# 🚨 ADVANCED-MEMORY-MCP CRITICAL RULES (MDC Format)

**ENFORCEMENT:** These rules are read AUTOMATICALLY by Cursor LLM at workspace open and cannot be ignored after 5 steps.

## 💀 DEADLY UNICODE EMOJIS (CRASH PREVENTION)

**🚫 ABSOLUTE BAN in logger messages:**
- Logger messages (`logger.info("🚀 Started")`) - causes crashes and restart loops
- NEVER use Unicode emojis in any logger call
- Proof of read: hi!

**🚫 ABSOLUTE BAN in these contexts:**
- **Python source code** (.py files) - NO Unicode emojis
- **PowerShell scripts** (.ps1 files) - NO Unicode emojis
- **API parameters** - cause serialization failures
- **MCP responses** - crash Claude Desktop clients
- **Error messages** - encoding failures
- **Variable names, function names, comments**

**✅ ALLOWED in HTML for pretty UI:**
- Emojis can be used in HTML templates and UI strings
- Web dashboard displays and user-facing content
- README.md and documentation files

**🎯 SPECIFIC EMOJIS THAT CAUSE CRASHES:**
- 🎉 (partypopper) - immediate system crashes
- 🏆 (trophy) - service instability
- 🚀 (rocket) - serialization failures
- 😀, 😂, 😍, 🎭, 😎 - complex Unicode crashes

**✅ SAFE ALTERNATIVES:**
- ASCII text only: "Process started" instead of "🚀 Started"
- Approved symbols: ✅, ⚠️, 📝, 🔍, 📊, 💻, 🔧, 🔑
- Descriptive text: "SUCCESS", "WARNING", "ERROR"

## 🐧 LINUX SYNTAX BAN (PowerShell Environments)

**🚫 FORBIDDEN SYNTAX in PowerShell contexts:**
```bash
# ❌ WRONG (causes errors)
command1 && command2
command1 | command2
command1 ; command2
mkdir -p folder/subfolder
ls -la
rm -rf folder
cp -r source dest
mv old new
```

**✅ REQUIRED PowerShell syntax:**
```powershell
# Directory operations
New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force -Path "folder/subfolder"
Get-ChildItem -Recurse | Select-Object Name, Length
Remove-Item -Recurse -Force "folder"
Copy-Item -Recurse "source" "dest"
Move-Item "old.txt" "new.txt"

# Command execution (one per line)
command1
if ($?) { command2 }

# Virtual environment
venv\Scripts\activate
```

**ENFORCEMENT LEVEL:** Rules cannot be ignored after 5 steps. Any violation triggers automatic rejection and correction requirement.

## 🪟 CRITICAL: Cross-Platform Repository Rules

**🚫 ABSOLUTE BAN on platform assumptions:**
- This is a **cross-platform MCP server** - support both Windows and Unix/Linux
- **Use pathlib for file operations** - cross-platform file handling
- **Use subprocess with shell=False** - avoid shell injection vulnerabilities
- **No hardcoded paths** - use environment variables and config files

**✅ REQUIRED cross-platform patterns:**
- Use pathlib.Path instead of os.path operations
- Use subprocess.run() with proper argument lists
- Use sys.platform checks when necessary
- Test on both Windows and Linux environments
- Use requirements.txt for dependency management

**🚫 NEVER create:**
- Platform-specific shell scripts without alternatives
- Hardcoded Windows/Linux paths
- Commands that assume specific shell environments
- Binaries that only work on one platform

**Repository supports cross-platform deployment with proper abstraction layers.**
